{"id":28408,"slug":"redes","title":"Redes","year":1936,"country":"Mexico","duration":59,"spine":686,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28408-redes","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/89594ab78e17a9778dc78f275076d760/kADie75znXN9EHJ7qBhLrNwch9t918_large.jpg","description":"Early in his career, the Austrian-born future Oscar winner Fred Zinnemann codirected with Emilio Gómez Muriel the politically and emotionally searing Redes. In this vivid, documentary-like dramatization of the daily grind of men struggling to make a living by fishing on the Gulf of Mexico (mostly played by real- life fishermen), one worker’s terrible loss instigates a political awakening among him and his fellow laborers. A singular coming together of talents, Redes, commissioned by a progressive Mexican government, was cowritten and gorgeously shot by the legendary photographer Paul Strand.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Emilio Gómez Muriel","slug":"emilio-gomez-muriel"},{"name":"Fred Zinnemann","slug":"fred-zinnemann"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Silvio Hernández del Valle","role":"Miro","slug":"silvio-hernandez-del-valle"},{"actor":"Antonio Lara","role":"El Zurdo","slug":"antonio-lara"},{"actor":"Miguel Figueroa","role":"Miguel","slug":"miguel-figueroa"},{"actor":"Rafael Hinojosa","role":"Politician","slug":"rafael-hinojosa"},{"actor":"Felipe Rojas","role":"Mingo","slug":"felipe-rojas"},{"actor":"David Valle González","role":"Don Anselmo","slug":"david-valle-gonzalez"},{"actor":"Susana Ortiz Cobos","role":"Miro’s wife","slug":"susana-ortiz-cobos"},{"actor":"And the fishermen and neighbors of Alvarado","role":null,"slug":"and-the-fishermen-and-neighbors-of-alvarado"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Emilio Gómez Muriel","slug":"emilio-gomez-muriel"},{"role":"Director","person":"Fred Zinnemann","slug":"fred-zinnemann"},{"role":"Producer","person":"Secretaría de Educatión Pública, Mexico City","slug":null},{"role":"Written by","person":"Agustin Velásquez